# SimpleTest.finish starts cleanup before notifying test-complete

Firefox repository `git:314d8065c5ad68c7e5c5f92d`, revision `1a097ed8d31f6b307a5d0ebc34a82ceaf7f3727b`. Scope: DOM Canvas WebGL conformance tests and the shared Mochitest harness. Languages in the cited files: JavaScript. File roles are listed in the metadata. No production WebGL implementation is claimed.

waitForExplicitFinish sets _stopOnLoad=false. SimpleTest.finish records duplicate-finish and expected-failure issues, clears timeout callbacks, snapshots testsLength, sets _alreadyFinished=true, and exits chaos mode if needed. It pops registered cleanup callbacks in reverse order. Synchronous cleanup exceptions become failed assertions; fulfilled cleanup promises continue the chain. A rejected cleanup promise records a failure in the shown branch without continuing executeCleanupFunction. After cleanup it checks remaining test state/service workers and eventually calls parentRunner.testFinished with the test array.

## Observer and unresolved consumers

The `test-complete` observer topic is directly observed at the dispatcher. This pass does not identify all listeners or establish that the topic means asynchronous cleanup has finished. The `parentRunner.testFinished` receiver body was not followed.

**Async completion:** SimpleTest.finish itself returns undefined. It can return before asynchronous cleanup completes. The test-complete observer notification at line 1608 follows starting cleanup, not necessarily finishing it. Parent-runner notification occurs in the nested finish callback.

**Ownership:** SimpleTest owns _cleanupFunctions, _timeoutFunctions and _tests. This chain does not explicitly release the inner frames or cached harness reference.

**Cleanup limit:** The shown branch flushes permissions and preferences when !parentRunner || parentRunner.showTestReport, then calls SimpleTest.showReport. Normal runner cleanup and frame release require following TestRunner. Parent runner and service-worker receiver implementations were not analyzed.

## Evidence

[`testing/mochitest/tests/SimpleTest/SimpleTest.js` — `SimpleTest.waitForExplicitFinish`, lines 828–830](https://github.com/mozilla-firefox/firefox/blob/1a097ed8d31f6b307a5d0ebc34a82ceaf7f3727b/testing/mochitest/tests/SimpleTest/SimpleTest.js#L828-L830). Exact excerpt from lines 828–830:

```javascript
SimpleTest.waitForExplicitFinish = function () {
  SimpleTest._stopOnLoad = false;
};
```

[`testing/mochitest/tests/SimpleTest/SimpleTest.js` — `SimpleTest.finish initial state`, lines 1421–1504](https://github.com/mozilla-firefox/firefox/blob/1a097ed8d31f6b307a5d0ebc34a82ceaf7f3727b/testing/mochitest/tests/SimpleTest/SimpleTest.js#L1421-L1504). Exact excerpt from lines 1481–1489:

```javascript
  SimpleTest._timeoutFunctions = [];

  SimpleTest.testsLength = SimpleTest._tests.length;

  SimpleTest._alreadyFinished = true;

  if (SimpleTest._inChaosMode) {
    SpecialPowers.DOMWindowUtils.leaveChaosMode();
    SimpleTest._inChaosMode = false;
```

[`testing/mochitest/tests/SimpleTest/SimpleTest.js` — `afterCleanup and nested finish`, lines 1505–1580](https://github.com/mozilla-firefox/firefox/blob/1a097ed8d31f6b307a5d0ebc34a82ceaf7f3727b/testing/mochitest/tests/SimpleTest/SimpleTest.js#L1505-L1580). Exact excerpt from lines 1559–1571:

```javascript
    function finish() {
      if (parentRunner) {
        /* We're running in an iframe, and the parent has a TestRunner */
        parentRunner.testFinished(SimpleTest._tests);
      }

      if (!parentRunner || parentRunner.showTestReport) {
        SpecialPowers.cleanupAllClipboard(window);
        SpecialPowers.flushPermissions(function () {
          SpecialPowers.flushPrefEnv(function () {
            SimpleTest.showReport();
          });
        });
```

[`testing/mochitest/tests/SimpleTest/SimpleTest.js` — `executeCleanupFunction; test-complete`, lines 1582–1609](https://github.com/mozilla-firefox/firefox/blob/1a097ed8d31f6b307a5d0ebc34a82ceaf7f3727b/testing/mochitest/tests/SimpleTest/SimpleTest.js#L1582-L1609). Exact excerpt from lines 1582–1608:

```javascript
  var executeCleanupFunction = function () {
    var func = SimpleTest._cleanupFunctions.pop();

    if (!func) {
      afterCleanup();
      return;
    }

    var ret;
    try {
      ret = func();
    } catch (ex) {
      SimpleTest.ok(false, "Cleanup function threw exception: " + ex);
    }

    if (ret && ret.constructor.name == "Promise") {
      ret.then(executeCleanupFunction, ex =>
        SimpleTest.ok(false, "Cleanup promise rejected: " + ex)
      );
    } else {
      executeCleanupFunction();
    }
  };

  executeCleanupFunction();

  SpecialPowers.notifyObservers(null, "test-complete");
```

## Test links and validation

**Direct source-defined check, narrow scope:** The [always-fail sentinel](3a5b3b5d-3324-4080-9187-3196bf4a7aed.md) checks the deliberately failed assertion route. Other forwarding details, duplicate completion, async cleanup, and preference restoration are not directly asserted by this sentinel. **Execution-only:** The [inactive-attribute target](09ff632c-c5e0-445c-a5de-440fb21349eb.md) enters the shared harness. Other possible test links remain unverified.

The cited implementation, callers, and applicable receiver bodies were read. An independent source review accepted this scoped relationship with its listed gaps. No Firefox or Thunderbird product tests, generator run, or build ran for this evidence. There is no runtime pass/fail result. No Thunderbird–Firefox call chain is added by this Firefox-only slice.

